function do not affect the caller's bindings. \\
Strong typing, no implicit coercion &
§4.5 &
\code{sem4}: argument-count error; \code{sem2}: formula with undeclared element;
type mismatches reported rather than silently coerced. \\
Name equivalence for domain types &
§4.5 &
\code{compound water} and a hypothetical second compound with the same formula
are distinct; the type checker distinguishes them by name. \\
Reaction balance at declaration time &
§4.4.2 &
\code{sem1}: checker rejects the unbalanced \code{bad\_water} reaction before
any statement executes. \\
\code{for}-in over Formula &
§4.4.1 &
\code{molar\_mass} iterates elements in first-appearance order (H then O for
H\textsubscript{2}O) producing correct sums. \\
\code{for}-in over ReactionSide &
§4.4.1 &
\code{total\_reactant\_mass} iterates the species of a reaction side; the
extended rule added in D1 §4.4 revision. \\
\code{for}-in over List &
§4.4.1 &
\code{classify\_mass} called four times for each compound in the list. \\
Division-by-zero runtime error &
§4.4 &
\code{rt1}: detected at run time with file, line, and message. \\
Index-out-of-range runtime error &
§4.5 &
\code{rt2}: detected at run time with file, line, index, and valid range. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
